|~ `::fn` and what is declared under it: the function, its constructor,
   the words that build it from the noun and the words that fill and read
   it, their refusals and their laws. The words of this source are written
   as their literal, the chain that builds a function folded into data,
   since none of them stands while the source runs; the chain builds every
   other word.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSBLD#fn], [QSBLD#kind]. ~|

:fn
  |~~ A function: the subject it runs on, the inputs it takes, the answer
      it gives, the refusals it pages and the facts they carry, the
      invariants it holds, its laws, and its recipe, code or a primitive of
      the host. It is built from the noun by commands, each a verb the
      function so far is the subject of, the recipe last:
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)`.
      `on` names the subject, its page and its kinds; `takes` an input, its
      name, its page, the place of the call it reads, `/0` the first object
      and `~(query /0 1)` the first or one, and its kinds; `returns` the
      answer, its page and its kinds; `throws` a refusal and its page;
      `carries` a fact a refusal carries, its page and its kinds; `holds`
      an invariant of an input or of the answer, its refusal, its page and
      its condition; `proves` a law of the function, its page and its
      query; and `impl` the recipe. An input holds the value of its kind
      the walk of its tags reaches, and a value of none is refused under
      the input. A word is a function named under a
      label, called by its function alone, and `apply` runs a function on
      its subject with a vector of arguments, as a call holds its objects,
      `5 | apply f [3]`. A function holds no scope: its recipe reads its
      inputs, its subject and the words of the tree, and a value it needs
      beside them is an input or is written in its code, which `fill` does.
      It prints as its literal, the chain folded into data, its commands in
      a quote and its recipe after it, and reads back from it.
      ::link~(::any/apply | doc) ::link~(::quote | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps
        |~~ The literal of a function, the quote of the commands of its
            signature and its recipe, a quote, a primitive, or null for a
            contract no call runs.
        ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotPairError
        |~~ The literal of a function is a pair, the commands of its
            signature and its recipe:
            `::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(add by)]`.
        ~~|
    | throws :SignatureNotCommandsError
        |~~ The signature of a function is a quote of the commands that
            build it, each with its objects: `on` a page and kinds,
            `takes` a name, a page, a place and kinds, `returns` a page
            and kinds, `throws` a name and a page, `carries` a name, a
            page and kinds, `holds` a name, a page and a condition, and
            `proves` a name, a page and a query. The name of an input is a
            name its recipe reads as a step, of one segment, beside
            `answer`, `subject` and the words of a literal; the name of a
            refusal, a fact and a law is read as a tag; a page is a doc, a
            place a path or a quote, and kinds a tag or a set of tags, or
            for an input a vector of one of them, the kinds of each
            element.
        ~~|
    | throws :NameDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ A name of a signature is declared once: an input, a refusal
            and an invariant each by its name, the subject and the answer
            by theirs, and an invariant names no refusal the kinds of its
            input name, `:by/KindNotTakenError`.
        ~~|
    | throws :NameUnderNoInputError
        |~~ A refusal or an invariant written with a path is named under
            an input taken before it or under the answer,
            `:by/TooBigError`, and an invariant is written with one.
        ~~|
    | throws :LawUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A law written with a path is named under a name the function
            declares before it: an input, a refusal, an invariant, a fact,
            the subject or the answer, the refusal an input's kinds name
            among them, `proves :by/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString …`.
        ~~|
    | throws :FactUnderNoNameError
        |~~ A fact is named under a name the function declares before it,
            the refusal that carries it, `carries :TooBigError/bound …`.
        ~~|
    | throws :RecipeNotCodeError
        |~~ The recipe is a quote, a primitive of the host, or null for a
            contract.
        ~~|
    | throws :RecipeMissingError
        |~~ A contract, a function with no recipe, runs nothing: `impl`
            gives it one, `| impl ~(add by)`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isBuiltByCommands
        |~~ A function is built from the noun. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | type | eq ::fn)
    | proves :printsAsItsLiteral
        |~~ A function prints as its commands and its recipe. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by) | print | eq "::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number) ~(add by)]")
    | proves :readsBackFromItsPrint
        |~~ The print of a function reads back as the function. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | :f it | print | parse | apply it | eq f)
    | proves :isAWordNamedUnderALabel
        |~~ A function named under a label is a word, called by its
            function.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)) | 5 | plus 3 | eq 8)
    | proves :pagesTheInputsOfAWord
        |~~ The page of an input is the page of its node under the word. ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) | ::number/plus/by | doc | content | trim | eq "How much.")
    | proves :runsAPrimitiveRecipe
        |~~ A function whose recipe is a primitive runs it, the word
            `fill` applied by its value as it is called.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | apply (::fn/fill | binding | get /value) [3] | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by))
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfAnInput
        |~~ An invariant written under an input refuses a value that
            breaks it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by)) [500]
          !| get [~(type) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/by/TooBigError 500])
    | proves :holdsTheInvariantsOfItsAnswer
        |~~ An invariant written under the answer refuses an answer that
            breaks it.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | holds :answer/TooBigError |~~ A number past ten. ~~| ~(lt 10) | impl ~(add 100))
          !| get [~(type) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/answer/TooBigError 105])
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfACondition
        |~~ A condition that fails answers its failure. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(get /nope) | impl ~(add by)) [3]
          !| type
          |  eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError)
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfAnObject
        |~~ An object computed at the call that failed is the answer,
            where no input that reads its place takes a quote.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by))
          | :number/one (::fn | returns |~~ One. ~~| ::number | impl ~(1))
          | :number/any (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(by))
          | :number/bare ~(1)
          | get [~(5 | plus (get /x) !| type) ~(5 | one (get /x) !| type) ~(5 | any (get /x) !| type) ~(5 | bare (get /x) !| type)]
          | every ~(eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError))
    | proves :PayloadNotPairError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no pair. ~~|
        ~(::fn[1] !| type | eq ::fn/PayloadNotPairError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAStepThatIsNoCommand
        |~~ A step of a recipe is no command of a signature. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(add 1) ~(add 1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesACommandWithNoObjects
        |~~ A command names its objects. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(returns) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAnInputWithNoPage
        |~~ An input names its page. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by /0) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAnObjectPastTheKinds
        |~~ An input takes no object after its kinds. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number 1) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAPageThatIsNoDoc
        |~~ A page is a doc. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by "How much." /0) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesANameThatIsNoKeyword
        |~~ The name of an input is a keyword. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes "by" |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAnInputNamedWithAPath
        |~~ The name of an input is one segment. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by/x |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAnInputNoStepReads
        |~~ The name of an input is one a step reads. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :"a b" |~~ How much. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAWordOfALiteralAsAnInput
        |~~ A word of a literal is no input, which a step would read as
            the value.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :null |~~ Nothing. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesARefusalNoTagReads
        |~~ The name of a refusal is one a tag reads. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(throws :"Too big" |~~ Too big. ~~|) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesTheAnswerAsAnInput
        |~~ The answer is no input. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :answer |~~ An answer. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesTheSubjectAsAnInput
        |~~ The subject is no input. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :subject |~~ A subject. ~~| /0) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesAPlaceThatIsNoPathOrQuote
        |~~ A place is a path or a quote. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| 0) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesKindsThatAreNoTags
        |~~ Kinds are tags. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 #[1]) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesKindsOfEachElementTwice
        |~~ The kinds of each element stand in the vector as one tag or
            one set.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 [::number ::string]) ~(add by)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :SignatureNotCommandsError/refusesASignatureThatIsNoQuote
        |~~ A signature is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::fn[[] ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/SignatureNotCommandsError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesTwoInputsOfOneName
        |~~ Two inputs of one name are refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | takes :by |~~ Again. ~~| /1) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameDeclaredTwiceError/refusesAnInvariantNamedAsTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ An invariant named as the refusal of its input's kinds is
            refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | holds :by/KindNotTakenError |~~ Positive. ~~| ~(gt 0)) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/NameDeclaredTwiceError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoInputError/refusesARefusalUnderNoInput
        |~~ A refusal under a name no input takes is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(throws :x/TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~|) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/NameUnderNoInputError)
    | proves :NameUnderNoInputError/refusesAnInvariantOfNoInput
        |~~ An invariant written with no path holds of nothing. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(holds :TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~| ~(lt 10)) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/NameUnderNoInputError)
    | proves :LawUnderNoNameError/refusesALawUnderNoName
        |~~ A law under a name the function does not declare is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(proves :x/holds |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true)) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/LawUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :FactUnderNoNameError/refusesAFactUnderNoName
        |~~ A fact under a name the function does not declare is refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(carries :x/y |~~ A y. ~~|) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/FactUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :FactUnderNoNameError/refusesAFactWithNoPath
        |~~ A fact is a fact of a refusal, written with its path. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~(carries :y |~~ A y. ~~|) ~(1)] !| type | eq ::fn/FactUnderNoNameError)
    | proves :RecipeNotCodeError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no recipe. ~~|
        ~(::fn[~() 5] !| type | eq ::fn/RecipeNotCodeError)
    | proves :RecipeMissingError/refusesAContract
        |~~ A function with no recipe is refused at its call. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0) [3] !| type | eq ::fn/RecipeMissingError)
    | tells :call
        |~~ The call of a function `apply` runs, which no word names: a
            refusal of its subject, its arguments, its inputs or its answer
            is named under it, `::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError`, as a word's is
            named under its address.
        ~~|
    | proves :call/refusesArgumentsPastItsInputs
        |~~ Arguments past the places its inputs read are refused. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) [1 2] !| type | eq ::fn/call/ArgsBeyondInputsError)
    | proves :call/refusesAnInputLeftOut
        |~~ An input whose place the arguments leave out is refused. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by)) !| type | eq ::fn/call/by/NotGivenError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:fn/on
  |~~ Names the subject of a function, its page and the kinds it serves,
      `::fn | on |~~ A number. ~~| ::number`: a function `apply` runs
      serves a subject of those kinds alone, and a word serves them beside
      the values of its label, the noun's own tag name for a word of the
      noun itself.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the subject. ~~| /0 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds of the subject, a tag or a set of tags; any value
            where none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /1 null) #[::null ::set ::tag]
    | returns |~~ The function with its subject. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `on` names the subject of the noun's function, `::fn | on …`,
            or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :servesTheKindsItNames
        |~~ A function serves a subject of the kinds `on` names and
            refuses another under its call, the kinds its `:expected`.
        ~~|
        ~(:f (::fn | on |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~(add 1))
          | get [~(5 | apply f) ~("x" | apply f !| get [~(type) /expected])]
          | eq [6 [::fn/call/SubjectKindNotTakenError #[::number]]])
    | proves :pagesTheSubjectOfAWord
        |~~ The page of the subject is the page of its node under the
            word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/inc (::fn | on |~~ The number to raise. ~~| | impl ~(add 1)) | ::number/inc/subject | doc | content | trim | eq "The number to raise.")
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | on |~~ A number. ~~| !| type | eq ::fn/on/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/takes
  |~~ Adds an input to a function: its name, its page, the place of the
      call it reads, and the kinds it holds where they are given, a value
      of none refused under the name of the input,
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number`. The place is a
      path into the arguments, `/0` the first and `/0/by` the key `by` of
      a map handed first, or a quote that reads them, `~(query /0 1)` the
      first or one.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :name
        |~~ The name of the input, which its recipe reads. ~~|
        /0 ::keyword
    | throws :name/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The name of an input is a keyword, `:by`. ~~|
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the input. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | throws :page/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The page of an input is a doc, `|~~ How much. ~~|`. ~~|
    | takes :place
        |~~ The place of the call the input reads, a path or a quote. ~~|
        /2 #[::path ::quote]
    | throws :place/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The place is a path, `/0`, or a quote that reads the
            arguments, `~(query /0 1)`.
        ~~|
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds the input holds, a tag or a set of tags, or a vector
            of one of them for the kinds of each element; any value where
            none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /3 null) #[::null ::set ::tag ::vec]
    | returns
        |~~ The function with the input after the ones it held. ~~|
        ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `takes` builds from the noun, `::fn | takes …`, or a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :addsAnInput
        |~~ An input is added by its name, its page and its place. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | params | map /name | eq [:by])
    | proves :holdsTheKinds
        |~~ An input of kinds refuses a value of none under its name. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by)) ["x"] !| type | eq ::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :holdsTheValueOfItsKind
        |~~ An input holds the value of its kind beneath the tags of what
            it is given.
        ~~|
        ~(:Width |~~ A width. ~~|
          | 5
          | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(by | type)) [::Width#3]
          | eq ::number)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfItsKinds
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of an input name is paged by them where
            `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "`by` holds a value of `::number`.")
    | proves :holdsTheKindsOfEachElement
        |~~ An input of the kinds of each element holds the value of its
            kind of each, beneath the tags it is given under.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 ::Width#2]] | eq [1 2])
    | proves :keepsASetOfElements
        |~~ A set an input of the kinds of each element holds stays a set.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [#[2 1]] | eq #[1 2])
    | proves :holdsAnyElement
        |~~ The kinds `::any` of each element ask for a vector alone. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::any] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 "a"]] | eq [1 "a"])
    | proves :refusesAnElementOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ An element of none of the kinds is refused with its index. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [[1 "a"]]
          !| get [~(type) /index]
          |  eq [::fn/call/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :refusesNoVectorOfElements
        |~~ A value that is no vector is refused where the input names the
            kinds of each element.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs)) [5] !| type | eq ::fn/call/xs/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfTheKindsOfEachElement
        |~~ The refusal the kinds of each element name is paged by them
            where `throws` gives it no page.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/w (::fn | takes :xs |~~ Values. ~~| /0 [::number] | impl ~(xs))
          | ::number/w/xs/ElementKindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "Each element of `xs` holds a value of `::number`.")
    | proves :readsAKeyOfAMap
        |~~ A path into the arguments reads an input by its key. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0/by | impl ~(add by)) [{:by 3}] | eq 8)
    | proves :givesADefault
        |~~ A place read by `query` gives a default. ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(query /0 1) | impl ~(add by)) | eq 6)
    | proves :answersTheFailureOfItsPlace
        |~~ A place that reads the arguments by code and fails answers its
            failure.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| ~(first | sub "x") | impl ~(add by)) [3]
          !| type
          |  eq ::number/sub/subtrahend/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAStepWrittenForItsQuote
        |~~ An object computed at the call that failed, where the input
            that reads its place takes a quote, is refused under its
            kinds.
        ~~|
        ~(:vec/each (::fn | takes :code |~~ The code. ~~| /0 ::quote | impl ~(map code))
          | [1 2]
          | each (add 1)
          !| type
          |  eq ::vec/each/code/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :refusesAStepWrittenForAQuoteOfTheArgsByItsPlace
        |~~ Where the input that reads the args whole takes quotes, an
            object that failed is refused by its place.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/w (::fn | takes :cs |~~ Codes. ~~| ~(it) [::quote] | impl ~(1))
          | 5
          | w ~(add 1) (get /x)
          !| get [~(type) /index]
          | eq [::number/w/cs/ElementKindNotTakenError 1])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 !| type | eq ::fn/takes/SubjectNotFnError)
    | proves :name/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString
        |~~ A name written as text is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes "by" |~~ How much. ~~| /0 !| type | eq ::fn/takes/name/KindNotTakenError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/returns
  |~~ Names the answer of a function, its page and its kinds, the tag or
      the set of tags it is brought to,
      `::fn | returns |~~ The sum. ~~| ::number`: an answer of one kind is
      made that kind by its constructor, and one of none of several is
      refused under the answer.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the answer. ~~| /0 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds of the answer, a tag or a set of tags. ~~|
        /1 #[::set ::tag]
    | returns |~~ The function with its answer. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `returns` names the answer of the noun's function,
            `::fn | returns …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :bringsTheAnswerUnderItsKind
        |~~ An answer of another kind is refused under the answer of the
            call, the kind its `:expected`.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~("x")) !| get [~(type) /expected] | eq [::fn/call/answer/KindNotTakenError #[::number]])
    | proves :refusesAnAnswerOfNoneOfItsKinds
        |~~ An answer of none of several kinds is refused under the answer
            of the call.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number or a string. ~~| #[::number ::string] | impl ~(gt 1))
          !| get [~(type) /actualValue]
          |  eq [::fn/call/answer/KindNotTakenError true])
    | proves :passesTheFailureOfTheRecipe
        |~~ A recipe that fails answers its failure, which no kind brings.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number | impl ~(get /nope)) !| type | eq ::path/SubjectHasNoPartsError)
    | proves :namesTheAnswerOfAWord
        |~~ The answer of a function named under a label is the answer of
            the word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/half (::fn | returns |~~ The half. ~~| ::number | impl ~(div 2)) | ::number/half | manifest | has ::number/half/answer)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | returns |~~ A number. ~~| ::number !| type | eq ::fn/returns/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/throws
  |~~ Names a refusal of a function and its page,
      `::fn | throws :TooBigError |~~ A sum past a bound. ~~|`, under an
      input or the answer where it is written with a path, the page of the
      refusal the kinds of an input name among them; under a label it is a
      refusal of the word.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the refusal. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the refusal. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | returns |~~ The function with the refusal. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `throws` names a refusal of the noun's function,
            `::fn | throws …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresARefusalOfAWord
        |~~ A refusal of a function named under a label is a refusal of
            the word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | throws :TooBigError |~~ A sum past a bound. ~~| | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus
          | manifest
          | has ::number/plus/TooBigError)
    | proves :pagesTheRefusalOfKinds
        |~~ A refusal the kinds of an input name takes the page `throws`
            gives it.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | throws :by/KindNotTakenError |~~ By is a number. ~~| | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "By is a number.")
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/throws :E |~~ An e. ~~| !| type | eq ::fn/throws/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/holds
  |~~ Writes an invariant of an input or of the answer: the refusal of a
      value that breaks it, named under the input or the answer, its page,
      and the condition the value answers true to,
      `| holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100)`.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :name
        |~~ The name of the refusal of a value that breaks it,
            `:by/TooBigError`.
        ~~|
        /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the refusal. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :condition
        |~~ The condition the value answers true to. ~~|
        /2 ::quote
    | returns |~~ The function with the invariant. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `holds` writes an invariant of the noun's function,
            `::fn | holds …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :writesAnInvariantOfAWord
        |~~ An invariant of a function named under a label is a node of
            the word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by))
          | 5
          | plus 500
          !| type
          |  eq ::number/plus/by/TooBigError)
    | proves :passesAValueThatKeepsIt
        |~~ A value that keeps every invariant of its input goes on to the
            recipe.
        ~~|
        ~(5 | apply (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | holds :by/TooBigError |~~ Under a hundred. ~~| ~(lt 100) | impl ~(add by)) [3] | eq 8)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/holds :x/E |~~ An e. ~~| ~(true) !| type | eq ::fn/holds/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/proves
  |~~ Writes a law of a function, the claim its name makes, its page and
      the query that proves it,
      `| proves :addsBy |~~ Five and three is eight. ~~| ~(5 | plus 3 | eq 8)`;
      under a label it is a law of the word, which `laws` and `runLaws`
      read, and a name written with a path lays it under an input, a
      refusal, a fact or the answer, the refusal an input's kinds name
      among them.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :name |~~ The name of the law. ~~| /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the law, the claim it proves. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :query
        |~~ The query that proves the claim, answering `true`. ~~|
        /2 ::quote
    | returns |~~ The function with the law. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `proves` writes a law of the noun's function,
            `::fn | proves …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :declaresALawOfAWord
        |~~ A law of a function named under a label is a law of the word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | proves :addsBy |~~ Five and three is eight. ~~| ~(5 | plus 3 | eq 8) | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :liesUnderTheRefusalOfAnInput
        |~~ A law written under the refusal an input's kinds name lies
            under it.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | proves :by/KindNotTakenError/refusesAString |~~ A string is refused. ~~| ~(5 | plus "x" !| type | eq ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError) | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/by/KindNotTakenError
          | runLaws
          | map /ok
          | eq [true])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/proves :x |~~ An x. ~~| ~(true) !| type | eq ::fn/proves/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/carries
  |~~ Names a fact a refusal of a function carries, its page and its
      kinds, `| carries :TooBigError/bound |~~ The bound. ~~| ::number`,
      under the name its path names, one declared before it, a refusal
      `throws` declares or the kinds of an input name among them; under
      a label it is a fact of the word's refusal, which a failure of it
      carries and its alert shows in the order its facts are named.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :name
        |~~ The name of the fact, under the refusal that carries it. ~~|
        /0 ::keyword
    | takes :page |~~ The page of the fact. ~~| /1 ::doc
    | takes :kinds
        |~~ The kinds of the fact, a tag or a set of tags; any value where
            none is given.
        ~~|
        ~(query /2 null) #[::null ::set ::tag]
    | returns |~~ The function with the fact. ~~| ::fn
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `carries` names a fact of the noun's function,
            `::fn | carries …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :pagesTheFactOfARefusalOfAWord
        |~~ A fact of a function named under a label lies under the
            refusal of the word.
        ~~|
        ~(:number/plus (::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | throws :TooBigError |~~ Too big. ~~| | carries :TooBigError/bound |~~ The bound. ~~| ::number | impl ~(add by))
          | ::number/plus/TooBigError/bound
          | doc
          | content
          | trim
          | eq "The bound.")
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/carries :E/x |~~ An x. ~~| !| type | eq ::fn/carries/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/impl
  |~~ Gives a function its recipe, the code or the primitive that answers
      for it, `| impl ~(add by)`; a function of no commands is its code,
      `::fn | impl ~(add 1)` answering `~(add 1)`.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(on
        |~~ The noun itself, which starts the function, or a function. ~~|
        ::tag
    | takes :recipe
        |~~ The recipe, a quote or a primitive of the host. ~~|
        /0 #[::builtin ::quote]
    | throws :recipe/KindNotTakenError
        |~~ The recipe is a quote, `~(add by)`, or a primitive,
            `::builtin{}`.
        ~~|
    | returns
        |~~ The function with its recipe, or the code of one of no
            commands.
        ~~|
        #[::fn ::quote]
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError
        |~~ `impl` gives the recipe of the noun's function,
            `::fn | impl …`, or of a function.
        ~~|
    | proves :answersTheCodeOfNoCommands
        |~~ A function of no commands is its code. ~~|
        ~(::fn | impl ~(add 1) | eq ~(add 1))
    | proves :recipe/KindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no recipe. ~~|
        ~(::fn | impl 5 !| type | eq ::fn/impl/recipe/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesAnotherTag
        |~~ A tag of another noun is refused. ~~|
        ~(::number | fn/impl ~(add 1) !| type | eq ::fn/impl/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/fill
  |~~ Writes the arguments of a call into the head of the code of a
      function, each input a declaration with its page of the value it
      reads from them, as its call reads it, a quote among them written
      as the data it is, and answers the code:
      `::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | fill 3`
      answers `~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by)`.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(takes :args
        |~~ The arguments, as a call holds its objects. ~~|
        ~(it)
    | returns |~~ The code, its inputs written at its head. ~~| ::quote
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError |~~ `fill` writes into a function. ~~|
    | throws :RecipeNotCodeError
        |~~ `fill` writes into code: a contract or a primitive has none. ~~|
    | proves :writesTheArguments
        |~~ The value goes into the head of the code. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~(add by) | fill 3 | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3 | add by))
    | proves :writesEachInput
        |~~ Each input goes into the head of the code in its order. ~~|
        ~(::fn
          | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0
          | takes :b |~~ A b. ~~| /1
          | impl ~(add a | add b)
          | fill 1 2
          | eq ~(:a |~~ An a. ~~| 1 | :b |~~ A b. ~~| 2 | add a | add b))
    | proves :writesIntoTheEmptyCode
        |~~ Into the empty code the value goes as its one declaration. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | impl ~() | fill 3 | eq ~(:by |~~ How much. ~~| 3))
    | proves :writesADocAsTheValue
        |~~ A doc goes into the head of the code in parentheses, the value
            of its input.
        ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :d |~~ A doc. ~~| /0 | impl ~(d | content) | fill |~~ x ~~|
          | eq ~(:d |~~ A doc. ~~| (|~~ x ~~|) | d | content))
    | proves :holdsTheKinds
        |~~ A value of none of the kinds of its input is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 ::number | impl ~(add by) | fill "x" !| type | eq ::fn/call/by/KindNotTakenError)
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no function. ~~|
        ~(5 | fill 3 !| type | eq ::fn/fill/SubjectNotFnError)
    | proves :RecipeNotCodeError/refusesAContract
        |~~ A function with no recipe is refused. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :by |~~ How much. ~~| /0 | fill 3 !| type | eq ::fn/fill/RecipeNotCodeError))
    ::builtin{}]

:fn/params
  |~~ Answers the inputs of a function, each a map of its name, its page,
      its place and its kinds as written, null where it names none.
  ~~|
  ::fn[~(returns |~~ The inputs, a map for each. ~~| ::vec
    | throws :SubjectNotFnError |~~ `params` reads a function. ~~|
    | proves :readsTheInputs
        |~~ The inputs come out by their names. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0 | returns |~~ A sum. ~~| ::number | impl ~(a) | params | map /name | eq [:a])
    | proves :readsTheKindsAsWritten
        |~~ The kinds of an input come out as written. ~~|
        ~(::fn | takes :a |~~ An a. ~~| /0 ::number | takes :b |~~ A b. ~~| /1 | params | map /kinds | eq [::number null])
    | proves :SubjectNotFnError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A number is no function. ~~|
        ~(5 | params !| type | eq ::fn/params/SubjectNotFnError))
    ::builtin{}]
